    ],
    "newLines": [
      "### REST API",
      "",
      "`GET /api/v1/articles` reads only stored classified/scored article metadata, never source pages.",
      "Parameters: `min_score` (finite 0..10, default 0), `published_after` (RFC3339, exclusive),",
      "`limit` (1..100, default 100), and `cursor` (opaque, at most 1024 bytes). Invalid or duplicate",
      "parameters and mismatched/tampered cursors return 400. The query has a five-second context deadline.",
      "The endpoint inherits the existing API middleware and does not enable cross-origin access.",
      "",
      "Response: `{ \"items\": [{ \"id\": \"123\", \"guid\": \"...\", \"title\": \"...\", \"url\": \"...\",",
      "\"score\": 8, \"publishedAt\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\", \"topics\": [],",
      "\"feed\": { \"id\": \"1\", \"title\": \"...\" } }], \"nextCursor\": null }`. IDs are decimal strings;",
      "no body, description, extraction, or summary is selected or returned.",
      "",
      "Pages use strict descending `(published, id)` keysets and the first request's maximum item ID,",
      "so subsequent inserts (including backdated ones) cannot leak into that traversal. This is an",
      "insertion boundary, not a frozen view of later edits/deletions/classification changes.",
      "Repeat the same normalized score/date filters with `nextCursor`; page size may change.",
      "A null `nextCursor` means exhaustion; omit the cursor (or use an empty one) to start again.",
      "Cursors are authenticated with an in-memory reader key and become invalid after a server restart.",
      "An empty result is `{ \"items\": [], \"nextCursor\": null }`.",
      ""
